# Re-opens a campaign that backdrop.scenario already authored, walks into its dungeon and
# reports the backdrop. Run it twice against two copies of that campaign, which is what
# proves the last two of issue #9's acceptance criteria:
#
#   cp -r /tmp/demo-campaign /tmp/demo-moved                 # the whole directory moves
#   rm /tmp/demo-broken/images/backdrop-source.png           # the picture goes missing
#
#   PNP_CONTROL=/tmp/pnp.sock cargo run -p campaign_editor -- <the copy> &
#   PNP_CONTROL=/tmp/pnp.sock cargo run -p campaign_editor --bin pnp-ctl -- run \
#       crates/campaign_editor/scenarios/backdrop-reopen.scenario
#
# Moved, `loaded` is true at the path it was never told about. Broken, `failed` is true,
# `observe world` still lists the feature, and the status line says which file it was.

ping
fixed-delta 0.016
step 60

tool select
click 30 30
enter-dungeon
step 30

observe image
observe world
observe input
